{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Partners and Songs From The Silver Screen appeal to my interest in polished vocals, musical standards, and soundtrack music, reflected in A Musical Affair, Stages, and my Downton Abbey listening.",
    "Down To My Last Bad Habit connects with the country side of my listening reflected in 747 and Golden, so it feels like a plausible next choice."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Christmas albums fit something I have enjoyed before, but I am not looking for seasonal music right now, so that connection does not make me want to choose them today.",
    "Playing With Fire, The Very Best Of, Awakening, and Road leave me unsure of a match; their titles alone do not establish the vocals, repertoire, or relaxing sound I would want."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My past Christmas listening seems to have been treated as an ongoing preference regardless of my current mood.",
    "A broad connection to my music history seems to count too much when I cannot identify what actually connects an album to the parts I enjoyed."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest interaction with relaxing classical music suggests that a calm listening mood deserves more attention alongside my vocal and country interests.",
    "The performer and song selection matter to my choices; an ambiguous album title gives me too little reason to commit, even if the music might suit me."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my vocal, soundtrack, and country interests, but lean too heavily on past holiday listening and give too little weight to my current mood and identifiable musical connections."
}"}
